
Computes a 64-bit perceptual hash (dHash) for each screenshot in the
browser, independent of OCR text, so it also catches duplicates of
annotated/marked-up screenshots that text-based matching misses.
Near-identical hashes (Hamming distance <= 8/64) are grouped and
surfaced under a new "Possible duplicates" section in the sidebar,
following the same suggest -> review -> decide pattern already used
for calendar suggestions.

Nothing is deleted automatically: reviewing a group opens every
screenshot side by side, pre-selects all but the newest for deletion,
and lets the user adjust the selection or dismiss the group ("keep
all", persisted locally so it isn't suggested again).

